From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0813: transfer_skip_scrambled: no EDRAM ownership transfer between render targets that lay their pixels out differently (Direct3D 12; native stream, zero-copy session 2 A)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; scratch/zerocopy2/DESIGN2.md section A, TESTPLAN2.md). Written without a build or
  a run: checked with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp and the units that
  include d3d12/render_target_cache.h; 0 errors, no warning on an added line. Applies after 0812 (W/sdk/src of unlock-2x 17b7bf2).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Session 1's transfer census: nearly every transfer at 2000p goes between render targets of another sample count, bits a
  pixel or pitch (1x D24FS8 <20t> -> 4x D24FS8 <13t>, 16F -> D24FS8, D24FS8 -> 4x 8888, 8888 <20t> -> 4x 8888 <13t>, ...), 38 a frame,
  104 MB read and 88 MB written, 130-160 stencil-bit passes over 35-39 host Mpx. For such a pair every destination pixel gets the
  bits of another pixel or sample of the source (the EDRAM address of a sample depends on the pitch at 32 bpp, the bits a pixel and
  the sample count): the console shows that garbage too. New cvar transfer_skip_scrambled (int bits, default 0 = every transfer as
  before, hot reload): 1 the sample count differs, 2 the bits a pixel differ, 4 the pitch differs -> the transfer is not made, the
  destination keeps what its own resource holds (its ownership changes as before). Kept always: transfers between targets of the
  same layout (also depth to colour and between formats: the same pixel's bits read another way, which this title does use: the
  census shows 4x D24S8 -> 4x 8888 at the same base and pitch, blended into), and those that differ in the base only (a shift by
  whole tiles). transfer_skip_scrambled_poison: the area left out is cleared instead (colour magenta; depth 0.5 and stencil 0xA5).
  `[transfer-skip-scrambled] ...` every 10 s: left out by difference, kept, host Mpx and MB not moved, stencil-bit passes not drawn.
  Also: 0811's census counts the rectangles of 64 bpp destinations with their own pitch in tiles (GetPitchTiles, as the transfers do;
  it used the 32 bpp pitch), and 0812's own-transfers check looks at the input array (the filtered one is a copy).
Bucket: REDO

0813-transfer-skip-scrambled.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy session 2).

